  data: {
    LLM: "Concentrate on remembering the tiles you've returned to the row. When those tiles cycle back to the right, you will know exactly what you hold.\n\nOpponent Memory: Watch what tiles your opponents flip and return. If you know an opponent has a 6-4 at the end of their row, try to keep the line ends away from 6 or 4 to block them.\n\nEnd-Line Control: If you know your upcoming tile is a double, try to play your current tile on an end that makes the other end match your double, maximizing your chance of a double-play next turn.",
